      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-225949",
      ":question/problem": "|  | Truth-preserving | Falsity-preserving | Self-dual | Monotonic | Affine |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f_{1}$ | Yes | No | No | No | No |\n| $f_{2}$ | Yes | Yes | No | Yes | No |\n| $f_{3}$ | No | Yes | No | No | No |\n\nConsider the Boolean functions $f_{1}, f_{2}, f_{3}$ whose properties are given in the table above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. ${f_{1}, f_{2}, f_{3}}$ is a functionally complete set\n2. ${f_{1}, f_{2}}$ is a functionally complete set\n3. ${f_{1}, f_{2}, f_{3}}$ is a minimal functionally complete set"
